---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const projects = (await getCollection('projects')).sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);
---
<Base>
<div class="wrap">
  <header class="top">
    <a class="name" href="#top">Samkit Jain</a>
    <nav aria-label="Sections"><ul>
      <li><a href="#research">Research</a></li>
      <li><a href="#projects">Projects</a></li>
      <li><a href="#background">Background</a></li>
      <li><a href="#contact">Contact</a></li>
    </ul></nav>
  </header>

  <main id="top">
    <div class="hero">
      <h1>I build ML systems and find out why they break.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Dalhousie Computer Science (Honours) graduate in Halifax. I've worked on reinforcement learning for cyber defence, intrusion detection and computer vision, and I build backends and cloud apps on AWS. I'm looking for software, ML and security roles anywhere in Canada.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn" href="resume.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Resume (PDF)</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/SamkitCodes" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/samkit-jain" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <figure class="field">
      <canvas id="queries" role="img" aria-label="3,000 dots, one per LLM query: 1,582 Remove Defender, 1,029 Analyse Op Server0, 122 Remove Op Server0, and 267 invalid or missing."></canvas>
      <figcaption>
        <p class="field-head">3,000 questions to an LLM teacher. Every valid answer fell into three recommendations.</p>
        <ul class="legend">
          <li><i style="background:var(--c1)"></i><b>1,582</b> Remove, Defender</li>
          <li><i style="background:var(--c2)"></i><b>1,029</b> Analyse, Op Server0</li>
          <li><i style="background:var(--c3)"></i><b>122</b> Remove, Op Server0</li>
          <li><i style="background:var(--dot)"></i><b>267</b> Invalid or missing</li>
        </ul>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <section id="research">
      <h2>Research</h2>
      <article class="case">
        <p class="label">HONOURS THESIS<br>JAN&ndash;APR 2026</p>
        <div>
          <h3>Hybrid reinforcement learning for autonomous cyber defence</h3>
          <p>I built an end-to-end system in PyTorch for CybORG Cage Challenge 2. A frozen cybersecurity LLM (Cyber-Risk-Llama-3-8B) acts as a teacher to a PPO agent with an Intrinsic Curiosity Module, through action masking and an auxiliary teacher-alignment loss.</p>
          <p>The hybrid did not beat the PPO-ICM baseline. Its teacher repeated a few recommendations instead of responding to the network state, which biased early training and helps explain the instability. This was a 300-episode run limited by compute, so it is a study of what went wrong, not a final verdict on the method.</p>
          <p class="tags">Supervised by Dr. Srinivas Sampalli, Dr. Jaume Manero and Dr. Darshana Upadhyay</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="case">
        <p class="label">NSERC USRA<br>MAY&ndash;AUG 2025<br>FOLLOW-UP 2026</p>
        <div>
          <h3>Do ML intrusion detectors work on networks they weren't trained on?</h3>
          <p>With an NSERC Undergraduate Student Research Award, I replicated Cantone et al. (IEEE Access, 2024). In 2026 I rebuilt it independently on four datasets with over 34 million network flows, matching 77 of the paper's top 78 selected features.</p>
          <p>The result: validating on the same dataset can't pick a model that transfers. Near-identical models scored anywhere from 0.03 to 0.48 MCC on another network, and duplicated flows, 23–27% of the 2018 data, inflated one model's score from 0.15 to 0.34.</p>
          <p class="tags">Supervised by Dr. Nur Zincir-Heywood and Dr. Adetokunbo Makanju</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section id="projects">
      <h2>Projects</h2>
      <ul class="projects">
        {projects.map(({ data }) => (
          <li>
            <h3>{data.title}</h3>
            <p>{data.summary}</p>
            <p class="tags">{data.stack.join(' · ')}</p>
            {data.link && <a href={data.link} rel="noopener">View project</a>}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p class="note">I also keep up algorithm practice in C++ in <a href="https://github.com/SamkitCodes/algogym" rel="noopener">AlgoGym</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="background">
      <h2>Background</h2>
      <article class="case">
        <p class="label">2022&ndash;2026</p>
        <div>
          <h3>Bachelor of Computer Science (Honours), Dalhousie University</h3>
          <p>GPA 3.77/4.30. Dean's List and Sexton Scholar. I also marked CSCI 3171 (Network Computing) in fall 2024.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="case">
        <p class="label">BEFORE CS</p>
        <div>
          <h3>National-level tennis</h3>
          <p>Ranked among the top 200 players in the All India Tennis Association rankings.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <dl class="skills" style="margin:28px 0 0">
        <div><dt class="label">LANGUAGES</dt><dd>C++, C, Python, Java, JavaScript/TypeScript, SQL, Kotlin, R, PHP</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="label">MACHINE LEARNING</dt><dd>PyTorch, TensorFlow, scikit-learn, YOLO (Ultralytics), OpenCV, Pandas, NumPy, Matplotlib</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="label">BACKEND &amp; WEB</dt><dd>Node.js, Express, React, REST APIs, JWT, HTML, CSS</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="label">CLOUD &amp; DEVOPS</dt><dd>AWS (EC2, Lambda, S3, DynamoDB, CloudFormation, VPC, Cognito, CloudFront, Rekognition), Docker, Git, Linux, Bash</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="label">DATABASES</dt><dd>PostgreSQL, MySQL, MongoDB, Firebase</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="label">CERTIFICATIONS</dt><dd>AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section id="contact">
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>I'm based in Halifax, Nova Scotia, open to roles anywhere in Canada, and authorized to work in Canada with no sponsorship required.</p>
      <div class="contact-row">
        <span class="email" id="email">samkitj00@gmail.com</span>
        <button class="copy" id="copy" type="button">Copy email</button>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>Samkit Jain, Halifax</footer>
</div>

  <script src="../scripts/home.js"></script>
</Base>
